userutiles
==========

The Unix command line of Zainium OS, written in Rust: coreutils, a growing
part of util-linux, and a few Zainium tools. 175+ programs, one binary per
tool, with no multi-call dispatcher and no uutils dependency. MISSING.md
lists what is left.

Paths go through usercore::zainium, which reads /overlayer/syshub on
Zainium OS and falls back to the usual places on any other Linux, so the
tools also build and test there.

Layout
------

    core/          shared code
    cmd/<name>/    one crate per tool
    scripts/       build, install and test

Building
--------

    ./scripts/build.sh
    cargo build --release -p user_ls       one tool
    cargo test --workspace
    PREFIX=/overlayer/syshub ./scripts/install.sh

